    "title": "Stateful lifecycle screens do not clear the strategy gate",
    "description": "Technical audit of fixed entry-persistence, executable profit-lock, and late-loss-cut mechanisms on the strict-42 clustered-loss cohort.",
    "generatedAt": "2026-07-15T03:27:09Z",
    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "title",
        "type": "markdown",
        "layout": "full",
        "body": "# Stateful lifecycle screens do not clear the strategy gate"
      },
      {
        "id": "technical_summary",
        "type": "markdown",
        "layout": "full",
        "sourceId": "lifecycle_audit",
        "body": "## Technical summary\n\nAll three fixed causal lifecycle mechanisms are **rejected before strategy integration**. Two-second entry persistence removed `13 / 17` known winners. The executable profit lock improved toxic-fold PnL by `+$2.91` but made three terminal winners negative; the 30-second late loss cut improved it by `+$7.08` but made two winners negative. No neighboring thresholds were searched. The retained strategy remains below A+, `live_ready=false`, and no strategy parameters changed."
      },
      {
        "id": "metrics",
        "type": "metric-strip",
        "layout": "full",
        "cardIds": [
          "screens_card",
          "persistence_card",
          "late_delta_card",
          "late_harm_card"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "fold_finding",
        "type": "markdown",
        "layout": "full",
        "sourceId": "lifecycle_audit",
        "body": "## Aggregate improvement is bought by sacrificing winners\n\nBoth executable exits improve the 13-fold aggregate and raise profitable folds from `3` to `5`, but the effect is not stable across folds. The profit lock worsens folds 29, 33, 35, and 40; the late cut drives fold 40 from `-$2.24` to `-$7.81`. The grouped bars show why an aggregate-only selection would be unsafe: neither rule dominates the unchanged baseline."
      },
      {
        "id": "fold_chart_block",
        "type": "chart",
        "layout": "full",
        "chartId": "fold_pnl_chart"
      },
      {
        "id": "screen_table_block",
        "type": "table",
        "layout": "full",
        "tableId": "screen_outcome_table"
      },
      {
        "id": "path_finding",
        "type": "markdown",
        "layout": "full",
        "sourceId": "lifecycle_audit",
        "body": "## Fixed post-entry marks do not separate winners from losses\n\nAt 60 seconds after fill, `7 / 29` available terminal winners and `7 / 10` losses have negative executable marks. At 90 seconds, 26 winners are positive, but three winners remain negative while seven losses are negative. A rescue deadline would therefore create known losses even before exact engine integration. The overlap supports stopping lifecycle-threshold tuning on this cohort."
      },
      {
        "id": "horizon_table_block",
        "type": "table",
        "layout": "full",
        "tableId": "horizon_table"
      },
      {
        "id": "a_plus_finding",
        "type": "markdown",
        "layout": "full",
        "sourceId": "strict_baseline",
        "body": "## A+ remains blocked despite positive full-history PnL\n\nThe unchanged 202 ms baseline has `102` trades and `+$13.54`, but Wilson lower is `0.6843 < 0.70`, profitable eligible reports are `19 < 20`, and the five-report loss burst is `4 > 2`. Because every lifecycle screen failed winner preservation, none earns an exact 42-fold counterfactual or promotion credit."
      },
      {
        "id": "a_plus_table_block",
        "type": "table",
        "layout": "full",
        "tableId": "a_plus_table"
      },
      {
        "id": "scope",
        "type": "markdown",
        "layout": "full",
        "sourceId": "lifecycle_audit",
        "body": "## Scope, data, and definitions\n\nEntry persistence uses exact trades plus one-Hz post-gate opportunity rows in the ten negative folds inside the maximum burst window. Exit screens use all 40 exact positions across folds 29–41 and their target-token PMXT v2 book/change paths. An executable mark is the full-size visible-bid FOK quote net of entry and hypothetical exit fees. Insufficient depth fails closed. The comparison baseline is each trade's exact held-to-resolution PnL."
      },
      {
        "id": "methodology",
        "type": "markdown",
        "layout": "full",
        "sourceId": "lifecycle_audit",
        "body": "## Registered design and execution model\n\nThe persistence rule rechecks once between two and three seconds, requires the same direction and fresh edge at least `0.07`, and rejects missing state. The profit lock arms at `+$0.50` and sells after a fall to `+$0.10`. The late cut marks once at close minus 30 seconds and sells only a negative position. Both exits apply the measured `202 ms` insertion delay, retain the signal-time worst visible bid as the FOK limit, charge the current binary fee on both sides, and wait one second after a failed attempt. Each rule had a winner-preservation gate declared before its screen."
      },
      {
        "id": "limitations",
        "type": "markdown",
        "layout": "full",
        "sourceId": "lifecycle_audit",
        "body": "## Limitations, uncertainty, and robustness\n\nThe exit results are standalone causal reconstructions, not integrated harness variants. That is intentional: a failing causal screen should not trigger production code or a costly 42-fold replay. The cohort is the known loss cluster and is not independent promotion evidence. No adjacent recheck delay, PnL threshold, or seconds-before-close value was searched after rejection. The newest fully resolved sample still contains too few warmed trades to validate a new strategy mechanism."
      },
      {
        "id": "next_steps",
        "type": "markdown",
        "layout": "full",
        "body": "## Recommended next step\n\n1. Keep the volatility-floor strategy research-only and leave live trading off.\n2. Do not implement or tune the rejected persistence, profit-lock, or late-loss-cut rules.\n3. Move to **trade-print-calibrated passive entry**, a distinct payoff-geometry mechanism: replace the fixed `0.65` maker fill probability with causal touch, opposite-side volume, queue, and adverse-selection evidence from retained PMXT trade events.\n4. Calibrate on older folds, freeze one maker-or-skip rule, and test the known loss cluster before any full 42-fold replay.\n5. Require unchanged A+ gates, both-half profitability, and a larger fresh fully resolved block before promotion credit."
      },
      {
        "id": "further_questions",
        "type": "markdown",
        "layout": "full",
        "body": "## Further questions\n\n- Can PMXT trade prints support an auditable passive-fill and queue model at the required one-tick price?\n- Does maker-or-skip improve loss-fold economics after accounting for missed winners and adverse selection?\n- How many additional fresh warmed markets are required before the new payoff geometry has meaningful promotion power?"
      }
    ],
